            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I had a very quick and naive go at reproducing this last night and failed to. If anything the 3.3.x code was slightly faster (although it was all pretty noisy). I think it's most likely that I've messed up and/or am doing it in non-ideal conditions. But I'm starting from a position of not completely trusting this (or that it's universal across all hardware/c compilers).\n\nThe basic idea that an exact type check should be faster than the type flags check sounds very plausible though.",
